    "created_at": "2016-03-07T12:50:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-07T16:31:44Z",
    "body": "I think `refresh` was just specified before the URL standard was written.\n\n| Test | WebKit | Chromium | Gecko | Edge |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [a href](http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/3964) | not stripped | stripped | stripped* | stripped |\n| [meta refresh](http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/3965) | not stripped | stripped | stripped* | stripped |\n\n*) Changed from not stripped in https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=241788\n\n(If the \"Rendered view\", after clicking the link (if applicable), says \"Example Domain\", then it's \"stripped\"; if it's \"software.hixie.ch File Not Found\", it's \"not stripped\".)\n\nIt seems to me we can remove the stripping in meta refresh, and file a bug for ~~Chromium to not strip in the scheme. (Except if Edge does strip, and we want to change the URL spec?)~~ [WebKit to also strip].\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
